    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d513">

                <pb facs="0734" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/864: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Marriner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-18T21:00:00+01:00">August 18, 1935—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 18—4:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>703. Have just been informed that negotiations over the Abyssinian affair have
                    broken down due to Mussolini’s intransigent attitude as communicated to Laval by
                    Aloisi this morning. The British delegation is preparing to leave tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marriner</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
